# API contract rules

- Shared request/response/event schemas live in `packages/contracts` when both frontend and backend need them.
- Use runtime validation schemas (prefer Zod unless the repository establishes another standard).
- Infer TypeScript types from schemas where practical to avoid schema/type drift.
- Never trust JSON purely because it satisfies a compile-time interface.
- Serialize `bigint` monetary values explicitly as decimal strings or a dedicated money DTO; native bigint must never reach JSON serialization directly.
- Public error contracts must use stable machine-readable codes plus safe human-readable messages.
- Version breaking public API changes deliberately.
